the rasteriser needs the fallback face, and it was the only one that did

Cyrillic and Arabic drew as NOTHING and accented Greek fell out of the middle of a word, because the
UI family resolves to TeX Gyre Heros here, a Helvetica clone with Latin and basic Greek. The
machinery to find a face that can draw a character went in with cocotron 0025, and this is what
finally connects it to the screen.

FOUR ATTEMPTS FAILED FIRST, all reverted, and the reason is one line.

  -[NSLayoutManager showPackedGlyphs:length:glyphRange:atPoint:font:color:printingAdjustment:]
  uses its FONT ARGUMENT FOR ADVANCES ONLY. The indices then go to
  CGContextShowGlyphsWithAdvances, whose face comes from the GRAPHICS STATE, and the graphics state
  is set once per attribute run inside drawSelectionAtPoint by
  [NSFontAttributeInDictionary(attributes) setInContext: context].

So every attempt that reconciled the font in _fontForGlyphRange: and _drawGlyphs: was reconciling a
variable the rasteriser never reads. Generation made indices in the substitute face and the
rasteriser drew them through the original one, which is mojibake: rows that had been blank came out
as Latin gibberish, and so did their ASCII prefixes.

  attempt 1  substitute in _fontForGlyphRange:, re-derive in _drawGlyphs:.  ABORTED, and #217 later
             showed that was a cross allocator free, not the design.
  attempt 2  the same after #217.  0 faults in 6, and MOJIBAKE.
  attempt 3  record the face per character index on the LAYOUT MANAGER.  Identical mojibake.
  attempt 4  the same table on the TEXT STORAGE.  Identical mojibake. NSStringDrawer is a thread
             shared singleton that REPLACES its one storage on every draw, so a table keyed by
             character index is stale by the next string on either object.
  attempt 5  no table: decide from the ATTRIBUTE RUN, whose effectiveRange is the same from every
             index inside it, so both sides agree by construction.  STILL mojibake, which is what
             finally sent me to read showPackedGlyphs and find that neither side mattered.

THE DECISION IS THE ATTRIBUTE RUN and it is taken in three places that must not disagree: glyph
generation and metrics through _fontForGlyphRange:, the advances in _drawGlyphs:, and the graphics
state in drawSelectionAtPoint. One face per run is also what the rasteriser wants, since it puts a
whole span through one FT_Face.

An all-ASCII run costs one compare per character and no lookup, and O2FontPatternCoveringCharacter
memoises by code point behind that. Sixty four characters bounds the scan, not the run: both sides
read the same first sixty four of the same run, so they still agree.

MEASURED, by looking at the Money Manager EX language list:

  before  ar(SA) blank, be(BY) blank, bg(BG) blank, el(GR) drew Ellinik (Ellda)
  after   ar(SA) al-arabiyya in Arabic script, be(BY) belaruskaya and bg(BG) balgarski in Cyrillic,
          el(GR) Ellinika (Ellada) COMPLETE with its accents

